<odoo>
    <!-- ``base.res_partner_rule`` (patched by ``partner_multi_company``'s
         post_init_hook to use ``company_ids``) always exempts any contact
         linked to an internal user (``partner_share = False``) from the
         company scoping, so a colleague's contact card, from another
         company or even the same one, stays visible to everyone. Global
         (no ``groups``) rules are ANDed together (see
         ``ir.rule._compute_domain``), so this rule tightens that exemption
         away without touching the existing one: it must still hold for the
         record to be visible, on top of the base rule.

         A non-exempt user (without ``base.group_system``) gets to see an
         internal-user contact if: it is not actually internal
         (``partner_share = True``, e.g. a portal customer, untouched by
         this rule), it is their own contact (safety net), it has been
         deliberately shared (blank ``company_ids``, same "shared"
         convention as the rest of the stack), or it belongs to their own
         company/companies and is not itself a system administrator's
         contact (``is_system_admin_contact``, see ``models/res_partner.py``,
         administrators stay hidden from regular colleagues, in their own
         company or any other). Holding ``base.group_system`` (the real
         Settings/Administration group, a stricter bar than the sibling
         ``multi_company_field_visible``'s ``base.group_multi_company``)
         exempts a user entirely: they see every contact, as before. -->
    <record id="res_partner_rule_restrict_cross_company" model="ir.rule">
        <field
            name="name"
        >res.partner: hide other-company and administrator contacts from regular users</field>
        <field name="model_id" ref="base.model_res_partner" />
        <field name="domain_force">
            ['|', '|', '|', '|', ('partner_share', '=', True), ('id', '=', user.partner_id.id), ('company_ids', '=', False), '&amp;', ('company_ids', 'in', company_ids), ('is_system_admin_contact', '=', False), (1, '=', 1) if user.has_group('base.group_system') else (0, '=', 1)]
        </field>
    </record>
</odoo>
